  - permanent
  - doubly stochastic matrix
  - nearly decomposable matrix
  - Foregger's conjecture
abstract: >-
  A sorry-free Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Sections 2-7 of Y. Lavi's
  2026 preprint on Foregger's conjecture on minimum permanents of nearly
  decomposable doubly stochastic matrices. It ends with the paper's Theorem
  1.1 proved from one explicit hypothesis that is assumed and not proved:
  Gurvits's degree-sensitive capacity inequality for permanents (Gurvits 2008;
  Laurent-Schrijver 2010, Corollary 1a). The main theorems depend only on
  Lean's standard axioms. Because Gurvits's inequality is not formalized, this
  is a machine-checked reduction of Theorem 1.1 to that inequality, not a
  complete machine-checked proof of Foregger's conjecture.
